It turns out there's an ancient version of Hack ported to the PDP-11 in
the Google Groups archive.  It's in five parts at:

http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources/msg/38c41e789a171deb?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources/msg/ec8ce597800a7b56?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources/msg/1b804cfcd0ab5c36?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources/msg/bc9a16f00ce3a006?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources/msg/0d20569f14322f2d?dmode=source

If these links come up broken, search net.sources for the subject "Hack
sources for PDP11/44 and PDP11/45".

A derivative of this was ported to something called PC/IX and is archived
at

http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources.games/msg/131a08698331ca0f?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources.games/msg/d60ab34317942292?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources.games/msg/cded2b7d91150779?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources.games/msg/61d8f977bf8ca82c?dmode=source
http://groups.google.com/group/net.sources.games/msg/9b92eeb97d706784?dmode=source

If these links come up broken, search net.sources.games for the subject
"PC/IX Hack".

This version of Hack does not have fortune cookies and consequently no
rumors file.  Whatever long-forgotten glitch caused the parts bearing the
rumors file to disappear from some other archived Hacks does not affect
this Hack.

Downloading and extracting the files reveals them to have broad
similarities to Hack 1.0.  In particular, it launches a separate program
called mklev to create the level files.  mklev was merged into the main
binary in Hack 1.0.2.

But this PDP-11 Hack is clearly much more primitive.  There are no
distinct roles, and fewer different objects than even Hack 1.0 had. 
Several monsters are different, including some that also occur in the
"hack121" binary on Ali Harlow's website.

I have yet to build a usable binary from these sources.

This is not the long-lost JF Hack; it was worked on by two programmers
apparently in the Netherlands and contains a number of additions,
including some features not found in Hack 1.0 or 1.0.1.  Still it seems to
be much closer to JF Hack than anything else known to survive as source.

What's especially curious is that this Hack has the giant eel in
essentially its modern form.  The then-current version of AEB Hack was
1.0.1, which did not have giant eels.  It appears that Dr. Brouwer was
aware of this version of Hack and lifted the giant eel from it; the giant
eel first appears in Hack 1.0.2.

